      "textEn": "261\n\nEven more scared. The child was playing with his father in his lap. Hiding the secret, they were born in the world with arrogance. 18. Meaning of the word\n\nBalam cha—child also; Tasyah—of that (Putana); Urasi—on the chest; Kridantam—busy in playing; Akutobhayam—fearless; Hota—being; Gopihya—all the Gopis; Turanam—quickly; Samabhyetya—coming and; Jagruh—lifted up; Jata-sambhramah—with the same affection. The boy Krishna was also playing fearlessly on the upper part of Putana's chest, and when\nthe Gopis saw the boy's wonderful performance, they were very delighted and moved forward\nand picked him up. Meaning: These are the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Krishna. Although Putana could increase or decrease her body with the power of yoga,\nand she could gain power accordingly, but no matter in what form God may be,\nthey remain equally powerful. Krishna is the real God because whether he is a child or a youth, he\nremains the same man, he does not need to become powerful through meditation or any other external effort.\nThere is no need.\nTherefore, when the mighty Putana grew her body, Krishna remained as a small child.\nAnd fearlessly, he kept playing on the upper part of her chest. Possessing six arms. God, whatever\nform they may be in, remains always complete with all their powers. Their powers are always complete. Various powers are heard. They can show all their powers in any situation. Yashodaro hini bhyam taha samam balasya sarvatra. Rakshanti vidadhire samyaggopuchchambhramanadibhih. 19. Meaning of the word\n\nYashoda-Rohinibhyam—Yashoda and Rohini, along with the mothers, who mainly took the responsibility of the child; Taah—other Gopis;\nSamam—as important as Yashoda and Rohini; Balasya—of the child; Sarvatra—from all dangers; Raksham—protection; Vidadhire—\nfacilitated; Samyak—in a good way; Go-Puchchha-Bhraman-Adibhih—by swinging the cradle..\n\nThereafter, Mother Yashoda and Rohini, along with other mature Gopis, stroked the child Shri Krishna's entire\nbody to provide full protection.\nMeaning: When Krishna escaped such a great danger, then Mother Yashoda and Rohini were mainly"
