      "textEn": "265\n\nLike God, the Yagya Bhuk, from whom all the evil planets are afraid, always protect you during your enjoyment. Dakinyo, yatudhanyshcha, kushmanda yevarbhakagraha. Ghosts, spirits, demons, and evil spirits. 27). Kotara Revati Jyeshta Putana Matrukadayah. This madness is the obstruction of the body, mind, and senses. 28 ”. Dream-sighted, great, destructive, old, and child-like. May all be destroyed, those who are deeply engrossed in the acceptance of Vishnu's name. 29. Meaning of the word\n\nDakinyah, yatudhanhyah, cha kushmandaah - witches, witches, enemies of children; ye-jo - these; arbhak-grahaah - inauspicious for children; bhuta - evil spirits; prita - ghosts; pishachah - evil spirits similar to ghosts; cha - also; yaksha - yaksha group; raksha - demon group;\nVinayaka - named after Vinayaka; Kotra - named after Kotra; Revati - named after Revati; Jyeshta - named after Jyeshta; Putana - named after Putana;\nMatrika-adhyah - Matrika etc. evil spirits; unmadaah - causing madness; ye-jo other; hi - without doubt; apasmaraah -\nCausing memory loss; body-life-senses - body, life, and senses; Druhah - causing distress; Swapna-drashtaah - those who bring bad dreams; Maha-utpataah - those who cause great calamities; Vriddhaah - experienced; Bal-grahaah cha - and those who attack children; Ye - these; Sarve - all; Nashyantu - may be destroyed; Te - they; Vishnuh - of Lord Vishnu; Naam-grahan - by taking the name; Bhiravah -\nbecome afraid..\n\nDakini, Yatudhani, and Kushmanda, these evil daines are the biggest enemies of children, and with evil spirits like ghosts,\ndemons, vampires, yakshas, demons, and Vinayak, along with Kotra, Revati, Jyeshtha, Putana,\nand daines like Matrika are always ready to cause pain to the body, life, and senses, which leads to loss of memory, madness, and bad dreams. They, like wicked experienced elders,\ncreate a particularly heavy uproar for children.\nBut by chanting the name of Lord Vishnu,\nthey can be destroyed 